{
 "definition": "Forward Transfer (Continual World / CKA-RL, Wolczyk et al.): FWT_i = (AUC_i - AUC_i^b)/(1 - AUC_i^b), where AUC_i is the normalized area under task i's greedy-score learning curve during its own training phase in the continual run, and AUC_i^b is the same area for a from-scratch single-task baseline on task i. AUC is a step-weighted trapezoid of normalized performance p(t) over the phase window, divided by window length (equal-time average). The baseline curve is evaluated over the SAME iteration window [lo,hi] as the CL phase (linear interpolation at endpoints).",
